{
 "content": [
  {
   "attrs": {
    "textAlign": "left"
   },
   "content": [
    {
     "marks": [
      {
       "attrs": {
        "color": "rgb(33, 37, 41)"
       },
       "type": "textStyle"
      }
     ],
     "text": "Now that we have learned about joint probabilities, we have all the tools we need to prove one of the most useful properties of Expectation: the fact that the expectation of a sum of random variables is equal to the sum of expectation (even if the variables are not independent). In other words:",
     "type": "text"
    }
   ],
   "type": "paragraph"
  },
  {
   "attrs": {
    "textAlign": "left"
   },
   "content": [
    {
     "marks": [
      {
       "attrs": {
        "color": "rgb(33, 37, 41)"
       },
       "type": "textStyle"
      }
     ],
     "text": "For any two random variables ",
     "type": "text"
    },
    {
     "attrs": {
      "showEditor": false,
      "value": "X"
     },
     "type": "math_inline"
    },
    {
     "text": " and ",
     "type": "text"
    },
    {
     "attrs": {
      "showEditor": false,
      "value": "Y"
     },
     "type": "math_inline"
    },
    {
     "text": ",",
     "type": "text"
    }
   ],
   "type": "paragraph"
  },
  {
   "attrs": {
    "rawTex": "\\begin{aligned}\nE[X+Y] = E[X] + E[Y]\n\\end{aligned}"
   },
   "type": "block-tex"
  },
  {
   "attrs": {
    "textAlign": "left"
   },
   "content": [
    {
     "marks": [
      {
       "attrs": {
        "color": "rgb(33, 37, 41)"
       },
       "type": "textStyle"
      }
     ],
     "text": "The proof is going to use the Law of Unconcious statistician (",
     "type": "text"
    },
    {
     "marks": [
      {
       "attrs": {
        "class": null,
        "href": "./expectation#lotus",
        "rel": "noopener noreferrer nofollow",
        "target": "_blank"
       },
       "type": "link"
      }
     ],
     "text": "LOTUS",
     "type": "text"
    },
    {
     "marks": [
      {
       "attrs": {
        "color": "rgb(33, 37, 41)"
       },
       "type": "textStyle"
      }
     ],
     "text": ") where the function is addition!",
     "type": "text"
    },
    {
     "text": " ",
     "type": "text"
    }
   ],
   "type": "paragraph"
  },
  {
   "content": [
    {
     "attrs": {
      "textAlign": "left"
     },
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "Proof: Expectation of Sums",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "attrs": {
      "textAlign": "left"
     },
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "Let ",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "attrs": {
        "showEditor": false,
        "value": "X"
       },
       "type": "math_inline"
      },
      {
       "text": " and ",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "attrs": {
        "showEditor": false,
        "value": "Y"
       },
       "type": "math_inline"
      },
      {
       "text": " be any two random variables:",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "attrs": {
      "rawTex": "\\begin{aligned}\n\n  \\E&[X+Y] \\\\\n  &= \\sum_{x} \\sum_{y} (x + y) \\cdot P(X=x, Y=y) && LOTUS\\\\\n  &= \\sum_{x} \\sum_{y} x \\cdot P(X=x, Y=y) + y \\cdot P(X=x, Y=y) && \\text{Distribute}\\\\\n  &= \\sum_{x} \\sum_{y} x \\cdot P(X=x, Y=y) + \\sum_{y} \\sum_{x} y \\cdot P(X=x, Y=y) && \\text{Rearrange Sums}\\\\\n  &= \\sum_{x} x \\sum_{y} P(X=x, Y=y) + \\sum_{y} y \\sum_{x} P(X=x, Y=y) && \\text{Factor Out}\\\\\n  &= \\sum_{x} x \\cdot P(X=x) + \\sum_{y} y \\cdot P(Y=y) && \\text{Def of Marginal}\\\\\n  &= \\E[X] + \\E[Y] && \\text{Def of Expectation}\n\\end{aligned}"
     },
     "type": "block-tex"
    }
   ],
   "type": "borderedBox"
  },
  {
   "attrs": {
    "textAlign": "left"
   },
   "content": [
    {
     "marks": [
      {
       "attrs": {
        "color": "rgb(33, 37, 41)"
       },
       "type": "textStyle"
      }
     ],
     "text": "At no point in the proof do we need to assume that ",
     "type": "text"
    },
    {
     "attrs": {
      "showEditor": false,
      "value": "X"
     },
     "type": "math_inline"
    },
    {
     "text": " ",
     "type": "text"
    },
    {
     "marks": [
      {
       "attrs": {
        "color": "rgb(33, 37, 41)"
       },
       "type": "textStyle"
      }
     ],
     "text": "and ",
     "type": "text"
    },
    {
     "attrs": {
      "showEditor": false,
      "value": "Y"
     },
     "type": "math_inline"
    },
    {
     "marks": [
      {
       "attrs": {
        "color": "rgb(33, 37, 41)"
       },
       "type": "textStyle"
      }
     ],
     "text": " are independent. In the second step the joint probability ends up in each sum, and in both cases, one of the sums ends up marginalizing over the joint probability!",
     "type": "text"
    }
   ],
   "type": "paragraph"
  },
  {
   "attrs": {
    "id": "",
    "level": "4",
    "textAlign": "left"
   },
   "type": "heading"
  },
  {
   "attrs": {
    "id": "demonstration-of-the-proof",
    "level": "2",
    "textAlign": "left"
   },
   "content": [
    {
     "text": "Demonstration of the Proof",
     "type": "text"
    }
   ],
   "type": "heading"
  },
  {
   "attrs": {
    "textAlign": "left"
   },
   "content": [
    {
     "marks": [
      {
       "attrs": {
        "color": "rgb(33, 37, 41)"
       },
       "type": "textStyle"
      }
     ],
     "text": "Here is an example to show the idea behind the proof. This table shows the joint probabilities ",
     "type": "text"
    },
    {
     "attrs": {
      "showEditor": false,
      "value": "P(X=x, Y=y)"
     },
     "type": "math_inline"
    },
    {
     "text": " ",
     "type": "text"
    },
    {
     "marks": [
      {
       "attrs": {
        "color": "rgb(33, 37, 41)"
       },
       "type": "textStyle"
      }
     ],
     "text": "for two random variables ",
     "type": "text"
    },
    {
     "attrs": {
      "showEditor": false,
      "value": "X"
     },
     "type": "math_inline"
    },
    {
     "text": " ",
     "type": "text"
    },
    {
     "marks": [
      {
       "attrs": {
        "color": "rgb(33, 37, 41)"
       },
       "type": "textStyle"
      }
     ],
     "text": "and ",
     "type": "text"
    },
    {
     "attrs": {
      "showEditor": false,
      "value": "Y"
     },
     "type": "math_inline"
    },
    {
     "text": " ",
     "type": "text"
    },
    {
     "marks": [
      {
       "attrs": {
        "color": "rgb(33, 37, 41)"
       },
       "type": "textStyle"
      }
     ],
     "text": "that are not independent. You will see how computing ",
     "type": "text"
    },
    {
     "attrs": {
      "showEditor": false,
      "value": "E[X+Y]"
     },
     "type": "math_inline"
    },
    {
     "text": " ",
     "type": "text"
    },
    {
     "marks": [
      {
       "attrs": {
        "color": "rgb(33, 37, 41)"
       },
       "type": "textStyle"
      }
     ],
     "text": "is the sum of terms that are used in ",
     "type": "text"
    },
    {
     "attrs": {
      "showEditor": false,
      "value": "E[X]"
     },
     "type": "math_inline"
    },
    {
     "text": " ",
     "type": "text"
    },
    {
     "marks": [
      {
       "attrs": {
        "color": "rgb(33, 37, 41)"
       },
       "type": "textStyle"
      }
     ],
     "text": "and ",
     "type": "text"
    },
    {
     "attrs": {
      "showEditor": false,
      "value": "E[Y]"
     },
     "type": "math_inline"
    },
    {
     "marks": [
      {
       "attrs": {
        "color": "rgb(33, 37, 41)"
       },
       "type": "textStyle"
      }
     ],
     "text": ".",
     "type": "text"
    }
   ],
   "type": "paragraph"
  },
  {
   "attrs": {
    "sourceBytes": 2491,
    "sourceSha256": "28152befb80d257ee742851a0259daf7ac3737fd85e77b51100c1687448a7dfd"
   },
   "type": "interactive-demo"
  },
  {
   "attrs": {
    "textAlign": "left"
   },
   "content": [
    {
     "marks": [
      {
       "attrs": {
        "color": "rgb(33, 37, 41)"
       },
       "type": "textStyle"
      }
     ],
     "text": "Aside: These two random variables can each only take on two values. Having only four values in the joint table will make it easier to gain intuition.",
     "type": "text"
    }
   ],
   "type": "paragraph"
  },
  {
   "attrs": {
    "textAlign": "left"
   },
   "type": "paragraph"
  },
  {
   "attrs": {
    "textAlign": "left"
   },
   "content": [
    {
     "marks": [
      {
       "attrs": {
        "color": "rgb(33, 37, 41)"
       },
       "type": "textStyle"
      },
      {
       "type": "bold"
      }
     ],
     "text": "Computing ",
     "type": "text"
    },
    {
     "attrs": {
      "showEditor": false,
      "value": "E[X]"
     },
     "type": "math_inline"
    },
    {
     "marks": [
      {
       "type": "bold"
      }
     ],
     "text": " using joint probabilities",
     "type": "text"
    }
   ],
   "type": "paragraph"
  },
  {
   "attrs": {
    "textAlign": "left"
   },
   "content": [
    {
     "marks": [
      {
       "attrs": {
        "color": "rgb(33, 37, 41)"
       },
       "type": "textStyle"
      }
     ],
     "text": "A key insight from the proof is that we can compute using values from the joint. To do this we are going to use ",
     "type": "text"
    },
    {
     "marks": [
      {
       "attrs": {
        "class": null,
        "href": "./marginalization",
        "rel": "noopener noreferrer nofollow",
        "target": "_blank"
       },
       "type": "link"
      }
     ],
     "text": "marginalization",
     "type": "text"
    },
    {
     "marks": [
      {
       "attrs": {
        "color": "rgb(33, 37, 41)"
       },
       "type": "textStyle"
      }
     ],
     "text": ":",
     "type": "text"
    }
   ],
   "type": "paragraph"
  },
  {
   "attrs": {
    "rawTex": "P(X = x) = \\sum_{y} P(X = x, Y = y)"
   },
   "type": "block-tex"
  },
  {
   "attrs": {
    "textAlign": "left"
   },
   "content": [
    {
     "marks": [
      {
       "attrs": {
        "color": "rgb(33, 37, 41)"
       },
       "type": "textStyle"
      }
     ],
     "text": "We can expand ",
     "type": "text"
    },
    {
     "attrs": {
      "showEditor": false,
      "value": "E[X]"
     },
     "type": "math_inline"
    },
    {
     "text": " ",
     "type": "text"
    },
    {
     "marks": [
      {
       "attrs": {
        "color": "rgb(33, 37, 41)"
       },
       "type": "textStyle"
      }
     ],
     "text": "so that it is calculated only using values from the joint probability table:",
     "type": "text"
    }
   ],
   "type": "paragraph"
  },
  {
   "attrs": {
    "rawTex": "\\begin{aligned}\nE[X] \n&= \\sum_{x} x \\cdot P(X = x) \\\\\n&= \\sum_{x} x \\cdot \\sum_{y} P(X = x, Y = y)  && \\text{Marginalization of }X\\\\\n&= \\sum_{x} \\sum_{y} x \\cdot P(X = x, Y = y)&& \\text{Distribute }y\\\\\n\\end{aligned}"
   },
   "type": "block-tex"
  },
  {
   "attrs": {
    "textAlign": "left"
   },
   "type": "paragraph"
  },
  {
   "attrs": {
    "sourceBytes": 3479,
    "sourceSha256": "7c7322d4dd32b4b662c8da7f804f32d9778406c6830ee03a0e41cd5c3da97bef"
   },
   "type": "interactive-demo"
  },
  {
   "attrs": {
    "textAlign": "left"
   },
   "content": [
    {
     "attrs": {
      "showEditor": false,
      "value": "E[X]"
     },
     "type": "math_inline"
    },
    {
     "marks": [
      {
       "attrs": {
        "color": "rgb(33, 37, 41)"
       },
       "type": "textStyle"
      }
     ],
     "text": " = 0.1 + 0.3 + 0.4 + 0.8 = 1.6",
     "type": "text"
    }
   ],
   "type": "paragraph"
  },
  {
   "attrs": {
    "textAlign": "left"
   },
   "type": "paragraph"
  },
  {
   "attrs": {
    "textAlign": "left"
   },
   "content": [
    {
     "marks": [
      {
       "attrs": {
        "color": "rgb(33, 37, 41)"
       },
       "type": "textStyle"
      },
      {
       "type": "bold"
      }
     ],
     "text": "Computing ",
     "type": "text"
    },
    {
     "attrs": {
      "showEditor": false,
      "value": "E[Y]"
     },
     "type": "math_inline"
    },
    {
     "marks": [
      {
       "type": "bold"
      }
     ],
     "text": " using joint probabilities:",
     "type": "text"
    }
   ],
   "type": "paragraph"
  },
  {
   "attrs": {
    "textAlign": "left"
   },
   "content": [
    {
     "marks": [
      {
       "attrs": {
        "color": "rgb(33, 37, 41)"
       },
       "type": "textStyle"
      }
     ],
     "text": "Similarly, we can compute ",
     "type": "text"
    },
    {
     "attrs": {
      "showEditor": false,
      "value": "E[Y]"
     },
     "type": "math_inline"
    },
    {
     "text": " ",
     "type": "text"
    },
    {
     "marks": [
      {
       "attrs": {
        "color": "rgb(33, 37, 41)"
       },
       "type": "textStyle"
      }
     ],
     "text": "using only values from the joint:",
     "type": "text"
    }
   ],
   "type": "paragraph"
  },
  {
   "attrs": {
    "rawTex": "\\begin{aligned}\nE[Y] \n&= \\sum_{y} y \\cdot P(Y = y) \\\\\n&= \\sum_{x} y \\cdot \\sum_{x} P(X = x, Y = y)  && \\text{Marginalization of }Y\\\\\n&= \\sum_{x} \\sum_{y} y \\cdot P(X = x, Y = y)&& \\text{Distribute }x\\\\\n\\end{aligned}"
   },
   "type": "block-tex"
  },
  {
   "attrs": {
    "sourceBytes": 3493,
    "sourceSha256": "b2f42193c05c880bf4860d480e05ce2d131cffa2014e53f0e829e0771c828264"
   },
   "type": "interactive-demo"
  },
  {
   "attrs": {
    "textAlign": "left"
   },
   "type": "paragraph"
  },
  {
   "attrs": {
    "textAlign": "left"
   },
   "content": [
    {
     "marks": [
      {
       "attrs": {
        "color": "rgb(33, 37, 41)"
       },
       "type": "textStyle"
      },
      {
       "type": "bold"
      }
     ],
     "text": "Computing ",
     "type": "text"
    },
    {
     "attrs": {
      "showEditor": false,
      "value": "E[X+Y]"
     },
     "type": "math_inline"
    },
    {
     "marks": [
      {
       "type": "bold"
      }
     ],
     "text": " using joint probabilities:",
     "type": "text"
    }
   ],
   "type": "paragraph"
  },
  {
   "attrs": {
    "textAlign": "left"
   },
   "content": [
    {
     "marks": [
      {
       "attrs": {
        "color": "rgb(33, 37, 41)"
       },
       "type": "textStyle"
      }
     ],
     "text": "We can rewrite ",
     "type": "text"
    },
    {
     "attrs": {
      "showEditor": false,
      "value": "E[X+Y]"
     },
     "type": "math_inline"
    },
    {
     "text": " ",
     "type": "text"
    },
    {
     "marks": [
      {
       "attrs": {
        "color": "rgb(33, 37, 41)"
       },
       "type": "textStyle"
      }
     ],
     "text": "to be the sum of terms used in the calculations of ",
     "type": "text"
    },
    {
     "attrs": {
      "showEditor": false,
      "value": "E[X]"
     },
     "type": "math_inline"
    },
    {
     "text": " ",
     "type": "text"
    },
    {
     "marks": [
      {
       "attrs": {
        "color": "rgb(33, 37, 41)"
       },
       "type": "textStyle"
      }
     ],
     "text": "and ",
     "type": "text"
    },
    {
     "attrs": {
      "showEditor": false,
      "value": "E[Y]"
     },
     "type": "math_inline"
    },
    {
     "text": " ",
     "type": "text"
    },
    {
     "marks": [
      {
       "attrs": {
        "color": "rgb(33, 37, 41)"
       },
       "type": "textStyle"
      }
     ],
     "text": "above:",
     "type": "text"
    }
   ],
   "type": "paragraph"
  },
  {
   "attrs": {
    "rawTex": "\\begin{aligned}\n  E[X + Y] \n  &= \\sum_{x,y}(x + y) \\cdot P(X = x, Y = y)\\\\\n  &= \\sum_{x,y} x \\cdot P(X = x, Y = y) + y\\cdot P(X = x, Y = y) \n\\end{aligned}"
   },
   "type": "block-tex"
  },
  {
   "attrs": {
    "textAlign": "left"
   },
   "content": [
    {
     "marks": [
      {
       "type": "italic"
      }
     ],
     "text": "Recall that ",
     "type": "text"
    },
    {
     "attrs": {
      "showEditor": false,
      "value": "P(x,y)"
     },
     "type": "math_inline"
    },
    {
     "text": " ",
     "type": "text"
    },
    {
     "marks": [
      {
       "type": "italic"
      }
     ],
     "text": "is shorthand for ",
     "type": "text"
    },
    {
     "attrs": {
      "showEditor": false,
      "value": "P(X=x, Y=y)"
     },
     "type": "math_inline"
    },
    {
     "marks": [
      {
       "type": "italic"
      }
     ],
     "text": ".",
     "type": "text"
    }
   ],
   "type": "paragraph"
  },
  {
   "attrs": {
    "textAlign": "left"
   },
   "content": [
    {
     "text": "Using the above derivation of the formula for ",
     "type": "text"
    },
    {
     "attrs": {
      "showEditor": false,
      "value": "E[X+Y]"
     },
     "type": "math_inline"
    },
    {
     "text": " in terms of values from the joint probability table:",
     "type": "text"
    }
   ],
   "type": "paragraph"
  },
  {
   "attrs": {
    "rawTex": "\\begin{aligned}\n  E[X + Y] = \\sum_{x,y} x \\cdot P(X = x, Y = y) + y\\cdot P(X = x, Y = y) \n  \\end{aligned}"
   },
   "type": "block-tex"
  },
  {
   "attrs": {
    "sourceBytes": 4673,
    "sourceSha256": "099c51aea31e5ae04553be651acaf264ea2ad66434806c02d5cff4a8917e7c6d"
   },
   "type": "interactive-demo"
  },
  {
   "attrs": {
    "textAlign": "left"
   },
   "content": [
    {
     "text": "Plugging in values:",
     "type": "text"
    },
    {
     "type": "hardBreak"
    },
    {
     "text": "E[",
     "type": "text"
    },
    {
     "attrs": {
      "showEditor": false,
      "value": "X+Y"
     },
     "type": "math_inline"
    },
    {
     "text": "] = ",
     "type": "text"
    },
    {
     "marks": [
      {
       "attrs": {
        "color": ""
       },
       "type": "textStyle"
      }
     ],
     "text": "0.1",
     "type": "text"
    },
    {
     "text": " + ",
     "type": "text"
    },
    {
     "marks": [
      {
       "attrs": {
        "color": ""
       },
       "type": "textStyle"
      }
     ],
     "text": "0.4",
     "type": "text"
    },
    {
     "text": " + ",
     "type": "text"
    },
    {
     "marks": [
      {
       "attrs": {
        "color": ""
       },
       "type": "textStyle"
      }
     ],
     "text": "0.3",
     "type": "text"
    },
    {
     "text": " + ",
     "type": "text"
    },
    {
     "marks": [
      {
       "attrs": {
        "color": ""
       },
       "type": "textStyle"
      }
     ],
     "text": "1.5",
     "type": "text"
    },
    {
     "text": " + ",
     "type": "text"
    },
    {
     "marks": [
      {
       "attrs": {
        "color": ""
       },
       "type": "textStyle"
      }
